    "body": "Apologies for the late response here. I'm generally not super happy with the current state of sniffing algorithms in this document, which is why I hoped we'd define CORB sniffing directly in Fetch in a newer algorithm style. As such I'm not entirely sure how to proceed. I want to find a way to test the existing algorithms better so we can figure out to what extent they are implemented and correct.\r\n\r\nI'm also no longer convinced only CORB should be sufficient to enable high resolution timers. Requiring CORS seems better, but it's still worthwhile to block as many of these \"no-cors\" loads as possible.",
